<title>USA: Unocal $80 mln settlement approved by judge.</title>
<headline>Unocal $80 mln settlement approved by judge.</headline>
<dateline>RODEO, Calif. 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A California judge over the weekend approved Unocal Corp's $80 million payment to residents injured by a 1994 toxic leak at the company's refinery near San Francisco, the company confirmed Monday.</p>
<p>Unocal, based in El Segundo, Calif., agreed in April to pay the settlement to 6,000 residents affected by the incident.</p>
<p>The refinery, bought in March by Tosco Corp, leaked catabarb over a two-week period in the summer of 1994.</p>
<p>Catabarb is a mixture of chemicals tha can cause respiratory problems, nausea, and skin irritations.</p>
</text>
